"Please help us keep this section updated and contribute your own error "
"resolutions, performance improvements, etc. Send in your helpful comments or "
"ideas 💡 to support@readthedocs.org or contribute directly by clicking :"
"guilabel:`Edit on GitHub` in the top right corner of this page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:6
msgid ""
"This guide provides some common errors and resolutions encountered in the :"
"doc:`build process </builds>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:9
msgid "Git errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:11
msgid ""
"In the examples below, we use ``github.com``, however error messages are "
"similar for GitLab, Bitbucket etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:15
msgid "terminal prompts disabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:17
msgid ""
"fatal: could not read Username for 'https://github.com': terminal prompts "
"disabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:21
msgid ""
"**Resolution:** This error can be quite misleading. It usually occurs when a "
"repository could not be found because of a typo in the repository name or "
"because the repository has been deleted. Verify your repository URL in :"
"guilabel:`Admin > Settings`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:23
msgid ""
"This error also occurs if you have changed a ``public`` repository to "
"``private`` and you are using ``https://`` in your git repository URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:27
msgid ""
"To use private repositories, you need a plan on `Read the Docs Business "
"<https://app.readthedocs.com>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:31
msgid "error: pathspec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:33
msgid "error: pathspec 'main' did not match any file(s) known to git"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:37
msgid ""
"**Resolution:** A specified branch does not exist in the git repository. "
"This might be because the git repository was recently created (and has no "
"commits nor branches) or because the default branch has changed name. If for "
"instance, the default branch on GitHub changed from ``master`` to ``main``, "
"you need to visit :guilabel:`Admin > Settings` to change the name of the "
"default branch that Read the Docs expects to find when cloning the "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:42
msgid "Permission denied (publickey)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:44
msgid ""
"git@github.com: Permission denied (publickey).\n"
"\n"
"fatal: Could not read from remote repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:50
msgid ""
"**Resolution:** The git repository URL points to a repository, user account "
"or organization that Read the Docs does not have credentials for. Verify "
"that the public SSH key from your Read the Docs project is installed as a "
"*deploy key* on your VCS (GitHub/GitLab/Bitbucket etc):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:54
#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:73
msgid "Navigate to :guilabel:`Admin > SSH Keys`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:55
#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:74
msgid "Copy the contents of the public key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:56
msgid ""
"Ensure that the key exists as a deploy key at your Git provider. Here are "
"direct links to access settings for verifying and changing deploy keys - "
"customize the URLs for your Git provider and repository details:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:58
#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:77
msgid "``https://github.com/<username>/<repo>/settings/keys``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:59
#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:78
msgid "``https://gitlab.com/<username>/<repo>/-/settings/repository``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:60
#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:79
msgid "``https://bitbucket.org/<username>/<repo>/admin/access-keys/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:64
msgid "ERROR: Repository not found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:66
msgid ""
"ERROR: Repository not found.\n"
"fatal: Could not read from remote repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:71
msgid ""
"**Resolution:** This error usually occurs on private git repositories that "
"no longer have the public SSH key from their Read the Docs project installed "
"as a *deploy key*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:75
msgid ""
"Ensure that the key exists as a deploy key at your Git provider. Here are "
"direct links to access settings for verifying and changing deploy keys - "
"customize the URLs for your VCS host and repository details:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:81
msgid ""
"This error is rare for public repositories. If your repository is public and "
"you see this error, it may be because you have specified a wrong domain or "
"forgotten a component in the path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:85
msgid "Build timeouts and out-of-memory errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:87
msgid ""
"If your build is cancelled with a message like ``Build exited due to time "
"out`` or ``Build exited due to excessive memory consumption``, your project "
"is exceeding the :ref:`build resource limits <builds:Build resources>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:91
msgid ""
"The following steps can help you stay within limits, in order of least to "
"most disruptive:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:93
msgid ""
"**Reduce the output formats you build.** Building ``htmlzip`` or ``pdf`` in "
"addition to ``html`` uses significantly more memory and time. You can "
"disable these in your :doc:`configuration file </config-file/v2>` using the :"
"ref:`formats <config-file/v2:formats>` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:98
msgid ""
"**Trim your documentation dependencies.** If you reuse your project's main "
"``requirements.txt`` for docs, create a separate, smaller requirements file "
"that only installs what Sphinx or MkDocs actually needs. See :doc:`/guides/"
"reproducible-builds` for guidance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:103
msgid ""
"**Switch from autodoc to autoapi.** If you are using ``sphinx.ext.autodoc`` "
"and installing your entire package to generate API docs, consider `sphinx-"
"autoapi`_ instead. It generates the same API documentation output by "
"statically analysing your source code, without needing to install or import "
"your package. This can dramatically reduce both memory usage and build time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:110
msgid ""
"**Use mamba instead of conda.** If your build uses conda, switching to :ref:"
"`mamba <guides/conda:Making builds faster with mamba>` reduces memory usage "
"and is faster at solving environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:114
msgid ""
"**Request a limit increase.** If none of the above steps help, you can email "
"support@readthedocs.org with your project URL and an explanation of why you "
"need more resources. On |com_brand|, contact support@readthedocs.com."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:123
msgid "Configuration file errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:125
msgid ""
"If your build fails with an error message that mentions ``.readthedocs."
"yaml``, the most common causes are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:128
msgid "**Invalid or unsupported setting**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:129
msgid ""
"Read the Docs validates every configuration file and will fail the build if "
"it encounters an unsupported key or an invalid value. Check the :doc:"
"`configuration file reference </config-file/v2>` to verify that all of your "
"settings are correct and supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:134
msgid "**Missing configuration file**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:135
msgid ""
"If you have enabled the requirement for a configuration file in your project "
"settings but the file does not exist in the repository (or is in the wrong "
"location), the build will fail. The file must be named ``.readthedocs.yaml`` "
"and placed at the root of your repository by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:141
msgid "**More than one configuration file found**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:142
msgid ""
"Only one ``.readthedocs.yaml`` file is expected per repository (unless you "
"are using a monorepo with a custom configuration path). If multiple "
"configuration files are detected in unexpected locations, remove the extras."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:147
msgid ""
"For a complete description of all available settings and their accepted "
"values, see the :doc:`configuration file reference </config-file/v2>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:152
msgid "General build failures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:154
msgid ""
"If your build fails without a clear error message related to your content or "
"configuration, it may be caused by a transient infrastructure issue on the "
"Read the Docs side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:158
msgid "**What to do:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:160
msgid ""
"Check the `Read the Docs status page`_ to see if there is an ongoing "
"incident."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:161
msgid ""
"Try triggering a new build by clicking :guilabel:`Build version` from your "
"project dashboard. Many transient failures resolve on a retry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:163
msgid ""
"If the problem persists, send an email to support@readthedocs.org (or "
"support@readthedocs.com for |com_brand|) and include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:166
msgid "The **project slug** (the name in the URL of your project dashboard)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:167
msgid ""
"The **build ID** from the failing build's URL (for example, in ``https://app."
"readthedocs.org/projects/myproject/builds/12345678/`` the build ID is "
"``12345678``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build-troubleshooting.rst:171
msgid ""
"Including the build ID lets the support team look up the exact logs for your "
"build, even if the failure is not visible in the UI."
msgstr ""
